    },
    {
      "id": "97046645-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "This agreement displays all lower-division courses required in the major : Stanislaus State courses or requirements on the left, approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right. Helpful resources: Academic Catalog Transfer Admissions Questions regarding this agreement may be directed to the Stanislaus State Articulation Analyst. Please visit the Stanislaus State Articulation Website for contact information.",
      "contentHtml": "<p>This agreement displays all<strong> lower-division courses required in the major</strong>: Stanislaus State courses or requirements on the left, approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Helpful resources: </strong></p><p><a href=\"https://catalog.csustan.edu/index.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Academic Catalog</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.csustan.edu/undergrad/transfer-admission\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Transfer Admissions</a></p><p><br></p><p>Questions regarding this agreement may be directed to the Stanislaus State Articulation Analyst. Please visit the <a href=\"https://www.csustan.edu/articulation\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Stanislaus State Articulation Website</a> for contact information.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "202e7445-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "About the Major",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ebc77645-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "Majors and/or minors in Modern Languages are designed to assist students as they plan careers. Some students anticipate teaching at the elementary or secondary level, while others are training to meet the challenges of advanced studies in language and literature. A growing number will discover that foreign language ability and sensitivity to other cultures are important assets, especially in career choices such as social sciences, the foreign service, international finance and banking, and international business. As today’s students gain knowledge and understanding of other languages and cultures, they inevitably develop greater appreciation of their own. In the process, they find themselves better equipped to succeed in our modern society where multilingual and multinational interests are becoming swiftly and inexorably part of our daily lives. View information for the Department of Philosophy and Modern Languages , including Learning Objectives for the department and its programs.",
      "contentHtml": "<p>Majors and/or minors in Modern Languages are designed to assist students as they plan careers. Some students anticipate teaching at the elementary or secondary level, while others are training to meet the challenges of advanced studies in language and literature. A growing number will discover that foreign language ability and sensitivity to other cultures are important assets, especially in career choices such as social sciences, the foreign service, international finance and banking, and international business.</p><p><br></p><p>As today’s students gain knowledge and understanding of other languages and cultures, they inevitably develop greater appreciation of their own. In the process, they find themselves better equipped to succeed in our modern society where multilingual and multinational interests are becoming swiftly and inexorably part of our daily lives.</p><p><br></p><p>View information for the <a href=\"https://catalog.csustan.edu/preview_entity.php?catoid=35&amp;ent_oid=1724\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Department of Philosophy and Modern Languages</a>, including Learning Objectives for the department and its programs.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "f4e27145-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 4,
      "content": "About Lower Division Major Requirements",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "b1b67645-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 5,
      "content": "No more than 8 units of Credit/No Credit-graded course work in courses graded exclusively Credit/No Credit may apply toward the major. A student who can demonstrate equivalent preparation may be exempt from 4 to 14 units of the lower-division requirement. Two years of college-level Spanish or the equivalent is required for admission to upper-division courses. Completion of an academic minor in a related discipline is not required, but is strongly recommended for single subject credential candidates.",
      "contentHtml": "<p>No more than 8 units of Credit/No Credit-graded course work in courses graded exclusively Credit/No Credit may apply toward the major.</p><p><br></p><p>A student who can demonstrate equivalent preparation may be exempt from 4 to 14 units of the lower-division requirement. Two years of college-level Spanish or the equivalent is required for admission to upper-division courses.</p><p><br></p><p>Completion of an academic minor in a related discipline is not required, but is strongly recommended for single subject credential candidates.</p>"
    }
  ],
